1. TWO WINDOWS, ONE LOCAL TERMINAL and ONE REMOTE TERMINAL
2. REMOTE WINDOW: git init --bare hello
3. LOCAL WINDOW: scp <user>@<host>:hello/HEAD
    a. ALLOWS YOU TO GET A SPECIFIC FILE OVER SCP
4. LOCAL WINDOW: git clone <user>@<host>:hello
    a. CLONES THE WHOLE REPO
5. LOCAL WINDOW: NOW YOU CAN ADD FILES, git add, git commit, git push origin main

